# Infocom's own ZIP test for Version 6, driven from a menu: a letter or
# a digit picks a section, and return at "End of test" goes back to the
# menu. Every section is run except the two that want pictures, D and
# M, since the game has no picture file and asks for picture numbers
# without end. The sections that draw in windows (K, W, Y, 4, 5) come
# out as their text in printing order, which is what the stream can
# show. The timed reads in T run their interrupt once before the
# script's key, so each countdown prints one step.

! SEED=1
! GAME=zcode-checkers/ziptest-r13-s890619.z6

# S: a partial save and restore through an auxiliary file, which the
# stream keeps in memory. The game says nothing either way, so this is
# a check that it runs through.
S
>

# A: arithmetic; return skips the RANDOM check, which random.accept
# covers.
A
>
>

# L: looping and predicates.
L
>

# O: objects, properties, and tables.
O
>

# C: calls, stacks, catch and throw.
C
>

# P: printing and margins; no to the three MORE-counter tests, yes to
# the CR interrupt test.
P
>
>
>
Y
>

# R: a reentrant READ, given a command and then nothing.
R
hello world
>
>

# T: READ, COPYT and PRINTT, ZWSTR with a new word and then a known
# one, the timed READ, DIROUT in table mode, INPUT and the timed INPUT.
T
THE AA BBBB
xyzzy
>
a
>
>
>
>
>

# W: windows and displays, return through each operation; no to the
# VT100 font test.
W
>
>
>
>
>
>
>
>
>
>
>
>
>

# F: function keys: the cursor keys, F1, escape, and space to leave.
F
<up>
<down>
<left>
<right>
[133]
<escape>
<space>
>

# Y: the YZIP windows test.
Y
>
>

# 1: DIROUT wrapping at 40 units, which is ten characters; a word
# instead of a second width ends it.
1
40
x
>
>

# 2: user stacks: twelve characters pushed on a stack of ten, then
# space to leave.
2
ABCDEFGHIJKL
<space>
>
>

# 3: window info, all sixteen properties of windows 0 and 1.
3
0
0
16
Y
1
0
16
N
>

# 4: the scroll test: down, down, up, quit.
4
D
D
U
Q
>

# 5: multiwindows, window 1 given its own position, size, and
# attributes again in so many words, since release 12 takes an empty
# answer as zero and leaves the window unusable for what follows.
5
1
1
1
16
320
N
N
N
Y
>
>
>

# Z, B, U: the two character sets, and the two mixed.
Z
>
